# Environment variables understood by Banxing. All are optional: normal use
# is configured in the pet's "模型配置" window and stored (key encrypted) in
# %APPDATA%\Banxing\settings.json. These exist for development, CI and demos.
# The app does not read a .env file; set them in your shell.

# --- model (overrides the saved settings) ---
# The saved API key belongs to the service and base URL it was entered for. If
# BANXING_PROVIDER or BANXING_BASE_URL points anywhere else, the saved key is NOT used:
# set BANXING_API_KEY as well, or nothing is sent. Consent is per destination too: a
# new origin has to be agreed to (model settings window, or `--demo ... --agree ORIGIN`).
# Redirects from the service are never followed.
# BANXING_PROVIDER=mock                 # anthropic | openai | mock (offline stand-in, templates only)
# BANXING_MODEL=claude-fable-5-2        # blank = the provider's default
# BANXING_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com   # https only, except localhost
# BANXING_API_KEY=

# --- where the app keeps its files ---
# BANXING_HOME=C:\somewhere\else

# --- Codex ---
# CODEX_HOME=C:\Users\me\.codex         # sessions are read from %CODEX_HOME%\sessions
# BANXING_PROCESS_NAMES=codex.exe       # replaces the list of executables treated as Codex

# --- tests ---
# BANXING_LIVE=1                        # Windows: run the UI Automation stand-in tests
# BANXING_SHOTS=C:\temp\shots           # where tests/test_screens.py saves pictures of the pet's windows
